@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# steamrt-analyzer
+
+Offline inspection of a Steam client `steamclient.so`, without running Steam.
+
+The runtime does two things before any hook is placed:
+
+1. parses `.rodata*` for strings and `.data.rel.ro` for `typeinfo`/vtable pairs
+2. resolves interface map methods by looking for string references inside each
+   vtable slot function
+
+Both passes live in `src/decompiler.cpp`. This tool mirrors them in Python so a
+new client build can be checked on any machine, including Windows, before the
+code is touched.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Python 3.10+
+- `pip install capstone`
+
+## Usage
+
+```sh
+python analyze.py steamclient.so                    # ELF summary + SLSsteam interface tables
+python analyze.py steamclient.so --strings GetServerPipe
+python analyze.py steamclient.so --refs CheckAppOwnership
+python analyze.py steamclient.so --vtable 14IClientUserMap
+python analyze.py steamclient.so --scan "0F B7 CA 31 C0 3B 4B"
+```
+
+`--interfaces` prints the vtable index of every method `src/vftableinfo.cpp`
+depends on. On a build where an index moved, the reported number is the one to
+hardcode in the `SLS_VFT_INDEX` table.
+
+`--refs` prints the code addresses that reference a string. Walking back from
+there with the `.eh_frame` FDEs gives the function that owns it, which is how the
+pattern anchors for the new runtime were found.
+
+## Getting the client binaries
+
+The client package is public:
+
+```sh
+# steamrt64/steamclient.so and steamrt32/steamclient.so
+curl -O https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/client/bins_steamrt_ubuntu12.zip.05ace2ddaa811afa700efd8d4f3c35ce24554d7a
+unzip bins_steamrt_ubuntu12.zip 'steamrt64/*' 'steamrt32/*'
+
+# arm64 client
+curl -O https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/client/bins_steamrt_linuxarm64.zip.05ace2ddaa811afa700efd8d4f3c35ce24554d7a
+```
+
+Always check the download against the `sha2` in
+`https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/client/steam_client_ubuntu12` (or
+`steam_client_linuxarm64`) before trusting the analysis.
+
+## Limits
+
+- vtable slot walks stop at the first entry that is not a mapped address in the
+  image. A value that happens to look like a function offset can still extend a
+  table, so treat the size as an upper bound and trust indices near the start.
+- pointers and relocation addends are read through the section map
+  (virtual address to file offset); the two differ in every section of a real
+  `steamclient.so`.
+- interface method names are attributed from a bounded disassembly window
+  (3 KB) that stops at the first `ret`, `jmp` or `int3`. Overloaded or
+  tail-called wrappers can attribute a name to more than one index; the first
+  reference keeps the plain name and later ones get a numeric suffix, matching
+  the runtime's rename rule. Check the target address with `--vtable` before
+  hardcoding it.
+- `--scan` is a byte matcher, not the runtime's prologue walk. It reports the
+  last match the runtime would see, so a signature with more than one hit is a
+  bug in the signature, not in the tool. Confirm the resolved address against
+  the FDE start of the intended function.
